<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Theorem 1</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that the decision problem <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TRACK}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>TRACK</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TRACK}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> takes as input a video <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=(F_{0},\dots,F_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=(F_{0},\dots,F_{T})</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T{+}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T{+}1</annotation></semantics></math> frames on an <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\times W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\times W</annotation></semantics></math> pixel grid, where <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> are constants and the input length is
<math id="A2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\Theta(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\Theta(T)</annotation></semantics></math>, and asks whether the permutation <math id="A2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> from frame <math id="A2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> to frame <math id="A2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is the identity.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The input is assumed to satisfy the following conditions:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Localization.</span>
Each frame <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> contains exactly <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> object centers (grid coordinates), denoted as <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{t}=\{c_{t,1},\dots,c_{t,k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{t}=\{c_{t,1},\dots,c_{t,k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{0,\dots,T\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{0,\dots,T\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t,i}\in[H]\times[W]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t,i}\in[H]\times[W]</annotation></semantics></math>, and the <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> object centers can be recovered from each frame in <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{NC}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐍𝐂</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{NC}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Continuity.</span>
Each object center moves by at most a fixed distance <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> between consecutive frames, and any two centers within any single frame are at distance <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;2d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;2d</annotation></semantics></math>, where, for convenience, we take <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(\cdot,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(\cdot,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> to be the <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> (Manhattan) distance.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The conditions above are standard prerequisites to ensure that the problem is well-posed in controlled environments and are easily satisfied in practice. The localization condition ensures that object centers are efficiently recoverable; for example, using constant-size visual markers allows template matching in <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{NC}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐍𝐂</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{NC}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The continuity condition formalizes the constraint discussed earlier (Section <a href="#S2.SS1" title="2.1 Task Formulation ‣ 2 Data Generation ‣ Can Vision-Language Models Solve the Shell Game?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> and <a href="#S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" title="Metrics. ‣ 3.1 Experimental Setup ‣ 3 Experiment ‣ Can Vision-Language Models Solve the Shell Game?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>) to prevent ambiguity by guaranteeing a unique correspondence between objects in consecutive frames. Practically, this can be achieved by using a sufficiently high frame rate relative to object speeds, so that objects move only a small distance between adjacent frames. 
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TRACK}_{k}\in\mathbf{NC}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>TRACK</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝐍𝐂</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TRACK}_{k}\in\mathbf{NC}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We show that the permutation <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> can be computed in <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{NC}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐍𝐂</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{NC}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For each frame <math id="A2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, let the localization procedure output the set of <math id="A2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> distinct centers as grid coordinates.
Since <math id="A2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> are constants, each coordinate has constant bit-length. Hence, per-frame computations are constant-size.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{c}_{t,1},\dots,\hat{c}_{t,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{c}_{t,1},\dots,\hat{c}_{t,k}</annotation></semantics></math> be the centers sorted lexicographically by <math id="A2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., by <math id="A2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> coordinate, breaking ties by <math id="A2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>).
Since both <math id="A2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and the coordinate length are constant, this sorting is computable by a constant-size circuit for each frame.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the continuity condition, each <math id="A2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{c}_{t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{c}_{t,i}</annotation></semantics></math> has at least one successor <math id="A2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{c}_{t+1,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{c}_{t+1,j}</annotation></semantics></math> within distance <math id="A2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>.
Such a <math id="A2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> is unique. Suppose there exist distinct indices <math id="A2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq j^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq j^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(\hat{c}_{t,i},\hat{c}_{t+1,j})\leq d\qquad\text{and}\qquad\mathrm{dist}(\hat{c}_{t,i},\hat{c}_{t+1,j^{\prime}})\leq d," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(\hat{c}_{t,i},\hat{c}_{t+1,j})\leq d\qquad\text{and}\qquad\mathrm{dist}(\hat{c}_{t,i},\hat{c}_{t+1,j^{\prime}})\leq d,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">then</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(\hat{c}_{t+1,j},\hat{c}_{t+1,j^{\prime}})\leq 2d," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(\hat{c}_{t+1,j},\hat{c}_{t+1,j^{\prime}})\leq 2d,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">contradicting the continuity condition in frame <math id="A2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define <math id="A2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t}:[k]\to[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t}:[k]\to[k]</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t}(i)=j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t}(i)=j</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text"> is injective: Suppose <math id="A2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t}(i)=\pi_{t}(i^{\prime})=j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t}(i)=\pi_{t}(i^{\prime})=j</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq i^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq i^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(\hat{c}_{t,i},\hat{c}_{t+1,j})\leq d\qquad\text{and}\qquad\mathrm{dist}(\hat{c}_{t,i^{\prime}},\hat{c}_{t+1,j})\leq d," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(\hat{c}_{t,i},\hat{c}_{t+1,j})\leq d\qquad\text{and}\qquad\mathrm{dist}(\hat{c}_{t,i^{\prime}},\hat{c}_{t+1,j})\leq d,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">so</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(\hat{c}_{t,i},\hat{c}_{t,i^{\prime}})\leq 2d," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(\hat{c}_{t,i},\hat{c}_{t,i^{\prime}})\leq 2d,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">again contradicting the continuity condition, now in frame <math id="A2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus <math id="A2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is injective. Since <math id="A2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is an injective map from a finite set of size <math id="A2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> to itself, it is bijective, and hence <math id="A2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t}\in S_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t}\in S_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Because the coordinates have constant bit-length and <math id="A2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed, each predicate
<math id="A2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}(\hat{c}_{t,i},\hat{c}_{t+1,j})\leq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}(\hat{c}_{t,i},\hat{c}_{t+1,j})\leq d</annotation></semantics></math>
is computable by a constant-size circuit, and so is the selection of the unique <math id="A2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, each <math id="A2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is computable by a constant-size circuit.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">The induced global permutation is</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi=\pi_{T-1}\circ\cdots\circ\pi_{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi=\pi_{T-1}\circ\cdots\circ\pi_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed, composing two permutations in <math id="A2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is computable by a constant-size circuit.
Computing this product in a balanced binary tree gives depth <math id="A2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\log T)=O(\log n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\log T)=O(\log n)</annotation></semantics></math> and polynomial size.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, the localization step is in <math id="A2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{NC}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐍𝐂</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{NC}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> by assumption, and all per-frame sorting and matching operations are constant-size, repeated over <math id="A2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=\Theta(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\Theta(n)</annotation></semantics></math> frames. Thus the total size is polynomial, and the overall depth is <math id="A2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\log n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\log n)</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the global permutation can be computed in <math id="A2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{NC}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐍𝐂</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{NC}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed, checking whether the resulting permutation <math id="A2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is the identity is computable by a constant-size circuit. Hence, <math id="A2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TRACK}_{k}\in\mathbf{NC}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>TRACK</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝐍𝐂</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TRACK}_{k}\in\mathbf{NC}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{WORD}_{S_{5}}\leq_{\mathbf{AC}^{0}}\mathrm{TRACK}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>WORD</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>𝐀𝐂</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></msub><mi>TRACK</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{WORD}_{S_{5}}\leq_{\mathbf{AC}^{0}}\mathrm{TRACK}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for any fixed <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 5</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">We reduce from the word problem over <math id="A2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{5}</annotation></semantics></math> with generators</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{1}=(12),\qquad\tau_{2}=(23),\qquad\tau_{3}=(34),\qquad\tau_{4}=(45)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>12</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>23</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>34</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>45</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{1}=(12),\qquad\tau_{2}=(23),\qquad\tau_{3}=(34),\qquad\tau_{4}=(45),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">which is <math id="A2.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{NC}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐍𝐂</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{NC}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-complete.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix constants <math id="A2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L&gt;2d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L&gt;2d</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h&gt;d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h&gt;d</annotation></semantics></math>. Place the first five anchor positions at</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{i}=((i-1)L,0),\qquad i=1,2,3,4,5," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}=((i-1)L,0),\qquad i=1,2,3,4,5,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">so they lie on the same horizontal row and consecutive anchors are distance <math id="A2.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> apart. Place the remaining anchors</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{6},\dots,p_{k}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{6},\dots,p_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">at fixed positions at distance greater than <math id="A2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2d</annotation></semantics></math> from the region traversed by the gadget trajectories. Thus all inactive objects can remain stationary throughout the video without violating the continuity condition.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">We use only the first five anchors to simulate the generators of <math id="A2.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>; the remaining anchors are occupied by stationary objects. The objects are rendered as fixed constant-size bright templates on a black background, so the object centers can be recovered trivially and the localization condition is satisfied.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">For each <math id="A2.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,2,3,4\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,2,3,4\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we construct a constant-length gadget <math id="A2.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> that swaps the objects at <math id="A2.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math> and leaves all other objects fixed:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}=((i-1)L,0),\qquad p_{i+1}=(iL,0)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}=((i-1)L,0),\qquad p_{i+1}=(iL,0).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p18.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p18.2.1" class="ltx_text">The gadget moves the object at <math id="A2.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> along the three-segment path</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="((i-1)L,0)\to((i-1)L,h)\to(iL,h)\to(iL,0)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">((i-1)L,0)\to((i-1)L,h)\to(iL,h)\to(iL,0),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p18.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p18.3.1" class="ltx_text">and moves the object at <math id="A2.p18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math> along the three-segment path</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(iL,0)\to(iL,-h)\to((i-1)L,-h)\to((i-1)L,0)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(iL,0)\to(iL,-h)\to((i-1)L,-h)\to((i-1)L,0).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p18.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p18.4.1" class="ltx_text">All other objects remain fixed.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">These two moving objects travel on different horizontal rows, so their trajectories remain disjoint. Since the active rows are <math id="A2.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=h</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=-h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=-h</annotation></semantics></math>, and since the other anchors lie on <math id="A2.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=0</annotation></semantics></math> and are spaced by <math id="A2.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L&gt;2d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L&gt;2d</annotation></semantics></math>, choosing <math id="A2.p19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> and the inactive anchors as above ensures that at every moment any two distinct object centers are more than <math id="A2.p19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2d</annotation></semantics></math> apart. By subdividing each segment into a constant number of sufficiently short steps, we obtain a constant-length video in which every object moves by at most <math id="A2.p19.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> between consecutive frames. Hence, each gadget satisfies the continuity condition and realizes exactly the adjacent transposition <math id="A2.p19.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> on the first five objects, while acting as the identity on objects <math id="A2.p19.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6,\dots,k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6,\dots,k</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now let</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w=\tau_{a_{1}}\tau_{a_{2}}\cdots\tau_{a_{m}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=\tau_{a_{1}}\tau_{a_{2}}\cdots\tau_{a_{m}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p20.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p20.2.1" class="ltx_text">be an input word over <math id="A2.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\tau_{1},\tau_{2},\tau_{3},\tau_{4}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\tau_{1},\tau_{2},\tau_{3},\tau_{4}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We use the standard right-to-left composition convention, so the group element represented by <math id="A2.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[w]=\tau_{a_{m}}\circ\cdots\circ\tau_{a_{1}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[w]=\tau_{a_{m}}\circ\cdots\circ\tau_{a_{1}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p20.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p20.3.1" class="ltx_text">that is, <math id="A2.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{a_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{a_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> acts first, then <math id="A2.p20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{a_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{a_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and so on. We map <math id="A2.p20.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> to a video <math id="A2.p20.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(w)</annotation></semantics></math> by concatenating the gadgets</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{a_{1}},G_{a_{2}},\dots,G_{a_{m}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{a_{1}},G_{a_{2}},\dots,G_{a_{m}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p20.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p20.4.1" class="ltx_text">starting from the frame in which the <math id="A2.p20.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> objects occupy the anchors <math id="A2.p20.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1},\dots,p_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1},\dots,p_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">Each gadget ends with every object exactly at an anchor position, so the next gadget starts from the correct configuration. Therefore, the global permutation induced by the full video is exactly</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[w]=\tau_{a_{m}}\circ\cdots\circ\tau_{a_{1}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[w]=\tau_{a_{m}}\circ\cdots\circ\tau_{a_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p21.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p21.2.1" class="ltx_text">on the first five objects, and the identity on the remaining objects. Hence, the global permutation <math id="A2.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is the identity on all <math id="A2.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> objects if and only if the word <math id="A2.p21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> evaluates to the identity in <math id="A2.p21.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, the reduction is a constant-block substitution: each input symbol <math id="A2.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is replaced by the constant-length gadget <math id="A2.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the output video is computable from the input word by a uniform <math id="A2.p22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{AC}^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐀𝐂</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{AC}^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> reduction.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p23.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Can Vision-Language Models Solve the Shell Game?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text">Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ Can Vision-Language Models Solve the Shell Game?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> gives <math id="A2.p24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TRACK}_{k}\in\mathbf{NC}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>TRACK</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝐍𝐂</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TRACK}_{k}\in\mathbf{NC}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ Can Vision-Language Models Solve the Shell Game?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> gives <math id="A2.p24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{NC}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐍𝐂</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{NC}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-hardness for every fixed <math id="A2.p24.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 5</annotation></semantics></math> via an <math id="A2.p24.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{AC}^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐀𝐂</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{AC}^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> reduction from <math id="A2.p24.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{WORD}_{S_{5}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>WORD</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{WORD}_{S_{5}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is <math id="A2.p24.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{NC}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐍𝐂</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{NC}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-complete. Therefore, <math id="A2.p24.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TRACK}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>TRACK</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TRACK}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.p24.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{NC}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐍𝐂</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{NC}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-complete.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Quantitative Analysis</h2>

<figure id="A3.F11" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.F11.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel" height="791.57" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 791.57" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,791.57) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;" fill="#4D4D4D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 6.74 L 0 784.84 C 0 788.56 3.02 791.57 6.74 791.57 L 543.26 791.57 C 546.98 791.57 550 788.56 550 784.84 L 550 6.74 C 550 3.02 546.98 0 543.26 0 L 6.74 0 C 3.02 0 0 3.02 0 6.74 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F7FFF7;" fill="#F7FFF7" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 6.74 L 0.83 768.2 L 549.17 768.2 L 549.17 6.74 C 549.17 3.47 546.53 0.83 543.26 0.83 L 6.74 0.83 C 3.47 0.83 0.83 3.47 0.83 6.74 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 18.6 776.43)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.23em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="445.97"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.F11.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.23em;">
<span id="A3.F11.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F11.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Gemini-3-Pro (Success Case)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 18.6 21.29)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.06em;--ltx-fo-height:52.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="731.83" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 729.14)" width="512.81"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.F11.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.06em;">
<span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Which cup contains the ball at the end of the video? 
<br class="ltx_break">(A) Left 
<br class="ltx_break">(B) Middle 
<br class="ltx_break">(C) Right 
<br class="ltx_break">Output your final answer (A, B, or C) in the format: <math id="A3.F11.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{&lt;option&gt;}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{&lt;option&gt;}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#000000;display:inline-block;"> </span>
<span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To determine which cup contains the ball at the end of the video, we can track the position of the cup with the ball through each swap:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. <span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Initial Position (00:00 - 00:01):</span> The video starts by lifting the <span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Left</span> cup, revealing the red ball underneath. The cup is then placed back down. <span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ball Position:</span> Left</span></span>
<span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. <span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">First Swap (00:02 - 00:03):</span> The cup in the Left position swaps with the cup in the Middle position. The ball moves from Left <math id="A3.F11.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Middle</span>.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3. <span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Second Swap (00:03 - 00:05):</span> The cup in the Middle position swaps with the cup in the Right position. The ball moves from Middle <math id="A3.F11.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Right</span>.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">4. <span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Third Swap (00:05 - 00:07):</span> The cup in the Right position swaps with the cup in the Left position (a long swap across the table). The ball moves from Right <math id="A3.F11.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Left</span>.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">5. <span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fourth Swap (00:07 - 00:09):</span> The cup in the Left position swaps with the cup in the Middle position. The ball moves from Left <math id="A3.F11.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.7.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Middle</span>.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">6. <span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fifth Swap (00:09 - 00:11):</span> The cup in the Middle position swaps with the cup in the Right position. The ball moves from Middle <math id="A3.F11.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.8.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Right</span>.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">At the end of the video, the cup containing the ball is in the <span id="A3.F11.pic1.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Right</span> position. <math id="A3.F11.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{C}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.F11.pic2" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel" height="708.94" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 708.94" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,708.94) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;" fill="#4D4D4D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 6.74 L 0 702.2 C 0 705.92 3.02 708.94 6.74 708.94 L 543.26 708.94 C 546.98 708.94 550 705.92 550 702.2 L 550 6.74 C 550 3.02 546.98 0 543.26 0 L 6.74 0 C 3.02 0 0 3.02 0 6.74 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFAFA;" fill="#FFFAFA" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 6.74 L 0.83 685.56 L 549.17 685.56 L 549.17 6.74 C 549.17 3.47 546.53 0.83 543.26 0.83 L 6.74 0.83 C 3.47 0.83 0.83 3.47 0.83 6.74 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 18.6 693.79)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.23em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="445.97"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.F11.pic2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.23em;">
<span id="A3.F11.pic2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F11.pic2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Gemini-3-Pro (Failure Case)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 18.6 21.29)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.06em;--ltx-fo-height:46.72em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="649.19" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 646.5)" width="512.81"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.F11.pic2.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.06em;">
<span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Which cup contains the ball at the end of the video? 
<br class="ltx_break">(A) Left 
<br class="ltx_break">(B) Middle 
<br class="ltx_break">(C) Right 
<br class="ltx_break">Output your final answer (A, B, or C) in the format: <math id="A3.F11.pic2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{&lt;option&gt;}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{&lt;option&gt;}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#000000;display:inline-block;"> </span>
<span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To find the location of the ball, let’s track the position of the cup containing the ball through each step of the video.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. <span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Start (00:00 - 00:01):</span> The ball is shown to be under the <span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Left</span> cup.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. <span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">First Swap (00:02 - 00:03):</span> <span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">The cup on the Left (containing the ball) swaps places with the cup in the Middle. <span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ball Position:</span> Middle.</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3. <span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Second Swap (00:04 - 00:05):</span> <span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.5.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">The cup in the Middle (containing the ball) swaps places with the cup on the Right. <span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ball Position:</span> Right.</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">4. <span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Third Swap (00:06 - 00:07):</span> <span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.6.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">The cup on the Right (containing the ball) swaps places with the cup in the Middle. <span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.6.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ball Position:</span> Middle.</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">5. <span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fourth Swap (00:08 - 00:09):</span> The cup in the Middle (containing the ball) swaps places with the cup on the Left. <span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.7.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ball Position:</span> Left.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">6. <span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fifth Swap (00:10 - 00:11):</span> The cup on the Left (containing the ball) swaps places with the cup in the Middle. <span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.8.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ball Position:</span> Middle.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F11.pic2.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">At the end of the video, the ball is under the cup in the middle position. <math id="A3.F11.pic2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{B}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>Examples of Gemini-3-Pro responses on the VET-Bench cups-game task. (Top) A successful case where the model correctly tracks all the intermediate states. (Bottom) A failure case where perception errors (highlighted in <span id="A3.F11.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">red</span>) lead to an incorrect final prediction.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F12" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.F12.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel" height="808.18" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 808.18" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,808.18) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;" fill="#4D4D4D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 6.74 L 0 801.44 C 0 805.16 3.02 808.18 6.74 808.18 L 543.26 808.18 C 546.98 808.18 550 805.16 550 801.44 L 550 6.74 C 550 3.02 546.98 0 543.26 0 L 6.74 0 C 3.02 0 0 3.02 0 6.74 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F7FFF7;" fill="#F7FFF7" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 6.74 L 0.83 784.81 L 549.17 784.81 L 549.17 6.74 C 549.17 3.47 546.53 0.83 543.26 0.83 L 6.74 0.83 C 3.47 0.83 0.83 3.47 0.83 6.74 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 18.6 793.03)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.23em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="445.97"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
